completion.summary:
`show REF --evaluations [--after CURSOR]` (MCP evaluations) lists the evaluation records of the item's active run, or of its latest run once none is active. Records are shown in run-feed order within the 12 KiB budget, with exact counts and a continuation bound to the item, run, read cut and policy. Each row gives:
- the record id and position, mode, evaluator session label, attempt key, time and revision;
- bounded verdict words with the exact omitted count;
- its own stale reason (an ended run's records are listed but not judged), what it supersedes, and whether it is the newest.

`show REF --evaluation RECORD_ID` (MCP evaluation) returns one record complete, with every verdict's criterion, rationale and citations and its evaluator provenance. There is no schema change, and completion and staleness are unchanged. Four review rounds were run; round 4 was clean from Codex and Claude on freeze 7ca257a3, and gate test-acd580b9 passed 9/9. Readiness reported all three stores ready. Commit 96c937d is pushed, and build 128b23a6fd62 is installed with the previous build backed up.
